{-# OPTIONS --guardedness #-}

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- COST EXPERIMENT for `Semantics.FailureSim` at REAL scale.
--
-- `PipePairFlipBFs` proves `bfServer≈DRhi : BFserverA l hi ≈DR bfServerSpec l hi`
-- through `DRFromRel`, which demands SIX obligations.  Since
-- `P ≈FD Q = (P ⊑FD Q) × (Q ⊑FD P)`, the SECOND component of
-- `drbisim→≈FD (bfServer≈DRhi l)` is `bfServerSpec l hi ⊑FD BFserverA l hi`
-- — the "spec is refined by the impl" half.
--
-- This module obtains exactly that half through the ONE-WAY route:
-- `FSimFromRel` reuses `PipePairFlipBFs`'s relation `BFSRel` and its FORWARD
-- obligations `bfsFwdE` / `bfsFwdT` / `bfsNdivL` VERBATIM (imported, not copied),
-- and replaces `bfsBwdE` / `bfsBwdT` / `bfsNdivR` by ONE stability obligation
-- `bfsStab`.  The three backward obligations are never mentioned.
--
-- `orientation-check` pins the direction claim mechanically.
--
-- No postulates, holes, or `NON_TERMINATING` in this module.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

